      ":question/id": "248e0ac0-8526-5585-b324-b2716f966f7a",
      ":question/problem": "Find the shortest distance between the point $(-3,-12)$ and the line $x=12.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's sketch the given situation.\n\n![](images/bd/bd3183f23f90f77689b54f70ab3520dd79284068efdf9fb376a3bfc94778bead.png)\n\nSince the line $x=12$ is a vertical line, the shortest distance between this line and the point $(-3,-12)$ is given by the absolute value of the difference between $x$-coordinate of the point and $12.$ \n\nSo, the shortest distance is\n\n$$\nd=|-3-12|=15.\n$$",
